.TH MCP-TERMINAL-DOCKER 1 "@VERSION@" "mcp-terminal-docker" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcp-terminal-docker \- control the MCP Terminal Docker container on the host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcp-terminal-docker
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mcp-terminal-docker
manages the \fBmcp-terminal\fR container and the \fBmcp-terminal-docker.service\fR
systemd unit.
.PP
Service JSON configuration:
.BR mcp-terminal-config (5)
(or
.BR "man 5 mcp-terminal-config" ).
.PP
The package pulls a versioned service image from Docker Hub, pulls sandbox worker
images (\fBpython-dev\fR, \fBnode-dev\fR, \fBbase-tools\fR), bind-mounts host
configuration and data directories, mounts the host Docker socket so the service
can spawn sandbox session containers, and starts the MCP Terminal HTTPS server
on port 3011 by default.
.PP
On \fBdpkg -i\fR / \fBapt install\fR / \fBapt upgrade\fR, maintainer scripts
automatically \fBdocker pull\fR the image tag from \fB/usr/lib/mcp-terminal/image-spec\fR,
pull sandbox images, and recreate the container so the running service matches
the installed package version.
.PP
Host log and data directories are owned by \fBmcp-terminal:mcp-terminal\fR
(see \fB/etc/default/mcp-terminal\fR). The service container runs with access
to \fB/var/run/docker.sock\fR to orchestrate sandbox containers on the host.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Start the systemd service (\fBsystemctl start mcp-terminal-docker.service\fR).
.TP
.B stop
Stop the systemd service.
.TP
.B restart
Restart the existing container instance without recreating it.
.TP
.B recreate
Stop, remove, and create the container. Use after changes to
\fB/etc/default/mcp-terminal\fR, \fB/etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json\fR, TLS
certificates, extra project bind mounts, or Docker network settings. Pulls the
package service image and sandbox images before recreate unless disabled in
\fB/etc/default/mcp-terminal\fR.
.TP
.B status
Show systemd unit status and \fBmcp-terminal-info\fR output.
.TP
.B info
Show host paths, Docker image tag, and container state.
.TP
.B help
Print usage (\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR).
.SH VALIDATION
Run \fBmcp-terminal-preflight\fR after configuration changes and before
reporting startup failures. The service logs the same runtime checks to
\fB/var/log/mcp-terminal/\fR on every start (errors abort startup; warnings are
logged only). See \fBmcp-terminal-config\fR(5) for the error catalog.
.SH PURGE
On \fBapt purge mcp-terminal-docker\fR, maintainer scripts stop systemd, remove the
container, and remove the saved Docker service image using
\fB/usr/lib/mcp-terminal/image-spec\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/default/mcp-terminal
Host-visible settings (port, paths, networks, extra bind mounts).
.TP
.B /etc/mcp-terminal/term_server.json
Service configuration bind-mounted read-only into the container.
.TP
.B /var/log/mcp-terminal
Application logs.
.TP
.B /var/mcp-terminal
Application data (session metadata, caches).
.TP
.B /etc/mcp-terminal/mtls_certificates
TLS certificates for HTTPS and MCP proxy registration.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/mcp-terminal/image-spec
Docker service image repository and tag baked at package build time.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/mcp-terminal/sandbox-images-spec
Sandbox worker image references pulled on install/upgrade.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcp-terminal-preflight (1),
.BR mcp-terminal-config (5),
.BR mcp-terminal-info (1),
.BR info (1),
.BR docker (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
